# Text assets the code embeds with include_str! (and parses) keep LF on
# every platform. A Windows checkout's default autocrlf turned the .ftl
# catalogs into CRLF, which broke a test that split them on "\n" (979a523,
# windows-latest). Source is normalised too, so a byte-level check
# (sha256 of a file) means the same thing on every machine.
*.rs   text eol=lf
*.ftl  text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.wgsl text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
# Asset files the starter library ships as pretty JSON and pins byte-for-
# byte on load -> save (umber-core smart.rs starter_*_roundtrip tests):
# a Windows CRLF checkout broke all twelve (windows-latest, 2026-11-06).
*.umbersmart  text eol=lf
*.umbermask   text eol=lf
*.umberbrush  text eol=lf
*.umberfilter text eol=lf
